From: Andriy Chuma <chuma.andriy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:34:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] block: Add the Create Flippies PC hard disk and floppy driver

The Create Flippies PC has two simple LBA disk controllers with DMA: the
hard disk and a 1.44 MB floppy drive. One command moves 1 to 256 sectors
of 512 bytes between the disk and one physically contiguous buffer and
interrupts when it is done.

flippies-hdd binds to both. It runs one request at a time through
blk-mq and gives the controller one command per contiguous segment. The
hard disk is fhda, with partitions. The floppy drive is fhdb: removable,
without partitions, read-only while the inserted disk is write
protected. Its controller interrupts on every insert and eject; the
driver then reads the new capacity and write protection and reports a
media change event, and the next open drops what was cached of the old
disk.
---
 drivers/block/Kconfig        |  11 +
 drivers/block/Makefile       |   1 +
 drivers/block/flippies-hdd.c | 442 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 454 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/block/flippies-hdd.c

